        // (T::ALL[0] -> 2 == max, T::ALL[1] -> 1 == MIDDLE, T::ALL[2]
        // -> 0 == min); T::ALL[1] is the SOLE inhabitant sitting
        // strictly between max `2` and min `0`, so the lex-order
        // complement projection MUST return the singleton
        // `vec![T::ALL[1]]` regardless of walk order (the ordering
        // axis DEGENERATES on the single-inhabitant middle band).
